data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

On this 64-bit system, each element is **8 bytes**. No `unsafe` context is needed — the `Span<T>` receiver makes `stackalloc` safe. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires `unsafe` since the size isn't fixed at compile time; use `nint.Size` instead.
